    </p><a href="/">← Home</a><pagefind-searchbox></pagefind-searchbox><script type="module" src="/pagefind/pagefind-component-ui.js"></script><script type="text/javascript" src="/static/pagefind.js"></script><h1 class="instruction-section" data-pagefind-body="1" data-pagefind-weight="10" data-pagefind-sort="title">SMC</h1><p class="insn_subtitle" data-pagefind-body="1">Secure monitor call</p>
      <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">This instruction causes an exception to EL3.</p>
      <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1"><span class="asm-code">SMC</span> is available only for software executing at EL1 or
higher. It is <span class="arm-defined-word">UNDEFINED</span> at EL0.</p>
      <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">If the values of <a class="armarm-xref" title="Reference to Armv8 ARM section" data-linkend="reg:aarch64-hcr_el2">HCR_EL2</a>.TSC and
SCR_EL3.SMD are both 0, execution of an
<span class="asm-code">SMC</span> instruction at EL1 or higher generates a Secure Monitor
Call exception, recording it in
<a class="armarm-xref" title="Reference to Armv8 ARM section" data-linkend="ESR_ELx">ESR_ELx</a>, using the EC syndrome value
0x17, that is taken to EL3.</p>
      <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">If the value of <a class="armarm-xref" title="Reference to Armv8 ARM section" data-linkend="reg:aarch64-hcr_el2">HCR_EL2</a>.TSC is 1 and EL2 is enabled in the current Security state, execution
of an <span class="asm-code">SMC</span> instruction at EL1 generates an
exception that is taken to EL2, regardless of the value of
SCR_EL3.SMD.</p>
      <p class="aml" data-pagefind-body="1">If the value of <a class="armarm-xref" title="Reference to Armv8 ARM section" data-linkend="reg:aarch64-hcr_el2">HCR_EL2</a>.TSC is 0 and the
value of SCR_EL3.SMD is 1, the SMC instruction
is <span class="arm-defined-word">UNDEFINED</span>.</p>
    
